  "title": "filter and find",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Keep only what you need\n\n`filter` returns every match. `find` returns the first match or `undefined`.\n\nFrom `[\"east\", \"south\", \"east\"]`, keep only `\"east\"`. Find the first beacon name that starts with `\"N\"`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "find-missing",
      "promptMd": "`[\"south\"].find(d => d === \"east\")` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "empty",
          "md": "`\"\"`"
        },
        {
          "id": "undef",
          "md": "`undefined`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "undef"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "only-east",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `onlyEast(dirs)` returns only `\"east\"` entries, joined as `east,east`. Print that.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "stdout",
          "equals": "east,east"
        },
        {
          "type": "ast",
          "query": "filter"
        },
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "dirs.filter(d => d === \"east\").join(\",\")"
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "function onlyEast(dirs) { return dirs.filter(d => d === \"east\").join(\",\") }\nconsole.log(onlyEast([\"east\", \"south\", \"east\"]))\nmodule.exports = { onlyEast }"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "Keep the items that match, or find the first one that does."
}
